{"kind":"artifact","text":"cmd/gs at ec453b92: merge succession with a legal citation path, an approval-bounded retirement authority, and the signer checked before Git is touched. requireApprovedImplementer requires the actor from --as to be the one the fold resolves as the approved head's implementer, or to hold ratifier; it runs after the approval checks and immediately before the receipt reservation, and again on the resume path, so a merge signed by anyone else is an ordinary refusal with the target, the reservation and the durable log untouched instead of a merge commit followed by a stranded succession. refuseUnreachableCrossAuthorRetirements still applies the fold's path-lineage bound before HEAD moves, and preflightSuccession still separates a succeeded retirement from one that orphans citations.","body":{"commit":"ec453b920460b2961a964c6b5d3921ca27e72d17","path":"cmd/gs"}}